  "result": "Perfect! All 147 tests pass \u2713 (133 original + 14 new). I've successfully added payment functionality:\n\n**src/payments.js (new file):**\n- `recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })` \u2014 Records a payment on an issued/partially-paid invoice:\n  - Validates invoice status is 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (NOT_ISSUED error)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n  - Validates date is in YYYY-MM-DD format (DATE_INVALID error)\n  - Validates payment doesn't exceed amount owed (OVERPAYMENT error)\n  - Creates payments array if missing\n  - Updates status to 'paid' when fully paid, 'partially_paid' when partial\n  - Returns new invoice without mutating original\n\n- `balanceDue(invoice)` \u2014 Calculates amount still owed:\n  - Returns total - sum of all payments\n  - Handles missing payments array\n  - Never returns negative (clamped at 0)\n\n**src/errors.js:**\n- Added `NOT_ISSUED`: Cannot record payment on draft invoice\n- Added `OVERPAYMENT`: Payment exceeds amount owed\n\n**test/payments.test.js (new file):**\n- 14 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - balanceDue calculations (with and without payments)\n  - Payment recording status updates (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n  - All error conditions (NOT_ISSUED, AMOUNT_INVALID, DATE_INVALID, OVERPAYMENT)\n  - Multiple partial payments\n  - Payments array creation and appending\n  - Immutability verification\n  - Edge cases (exact payment, zero balance)\n\nThe implementation ensures:\n- All amount calculations stay in cents (integers)\n- Status automatically transitions based on remaining balance\n- Original invoices are never mutated\n- Date validation uses the existing isValidDate utility",
